{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-25T16:58:26.181Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"The project directory exists at `/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/`. I created the six requested subdirectories; the existing `CDH17 Final Project.chat` file remains in place.\n\n**Directory structure**\n\n```text\nCDH17_Analysis/\n├── ai_documentation/\n├── data/\n├── figures/\n├── notebooks/\n├── results/\n├── scripts/\n└── CDH17 Final Project.chat\n```\n\n**Environment**\n\n| Component | Availability / version |\n|---|---|\n| Python | 3.14.4 |\n| pandas | 3.0.3 |\n| numpy | 2.4.4 |\n| scipy | 1.17.1 |\n| matplotlib | 3.10.8 |\n| seaborn | 0.13.2 |\n| requests | 2.33.0 |\n| Jupyter | CLI available; `jupyter_client` 8.9.1 and `jupyter_core` 5.9.1 are installed. Notebook, JupyterLab, and several other notebook components are unavailable. |\n\n**Connectivity and storage**\n\n- A request to the public GDC status endpoint succeeded with HTTP 200. It returned 221 bytes of status metadata; no datasets were downloaded.\n- Available disk space: **239 GB** on the filesystem containing the project directory.\n\nThe connectivity check confirms access to that GDC endpoint; it does not establish access to every public data source. I have not installed packages, downloaded datasets, or written the analysis pipeline.","date":"2026-11-25T16:58:45.073Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/CDH17 Final Project.chat","acp_log_key":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e:aff019f5-7f20-4441-a265-2ba9f03ae1d5","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e.aff019f5-7f20-4441-a265-2ba9f03ae1d5","acp_started_at_ms":1795625907285,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis","acp_account_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"aff019f5-7f20-4441-a265-2ba9f03ae1d5","thread_id":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e","parent_message_id":"9156dfb5-2fab-4971-bb55-461b94eeee3a","acp_thread_id":"01a213a4-fe33-7541-be04-ae44f8966e75","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":13804,"cached_input_tokens":12992,"output_tokens":513,"reasoning_output_tokens":191,"total_tokens":14317,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-25T17:00:42.570Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"## Feasibility finding\n\nUCSC Xena’s Toil hub has a **loaded, accessible gene expression matrix** containing TCGA, GTEx, and TARGET samples: **`TcgaTargetGtex_rsem_gene_tpm`**. The hub metadata identifies it as UCSC TOIL RNA-seq recompute gene expression, version 2016-09-03.\n\nI verified the hub’s metadata and made a one-byte range request to the compressed matrix endpoint. The file returned HTTP 206, with a total compressed size of **1,323,254,426 bytes** (about **1.32 GB / 1.23 GiB**). I did not download the matrix.\n\n## CDH17 and expression values\n\nThe matrix uses **versioned Ensembl gene IDs**, with a GENCODE v23 gene annotation map on hg38. The CDH17 feature is **`ENSG00000079112.9`**; an Ensembl lookup confirms that stable ID maps to CDH17.\n\nThe hub metadata describes the values as **RSEM TPM transformed to `log2(TPM + 0.001)`**. This is not `log2(TPM + 1)`. The metadata says TPM values were extracted and transformed, then combined; it does not document a batch-correction step.\n\n## Matching sample metadata and group definitions\n\nThe matching metadata dataset is **`TcgaTargetGTEX_phenotype.txt`**. Its fields include `sampleID`, `_study`, `_primary_site`, `_sample_type`, `detailed_category`, `primary disease or tissue`, and `_gender`. I checked the phenotype annotations against the expression sample IDs: all **19,131 of 19,131** had matching annotations.\n\nThese metadata fields distinguish the requested groups:\n\n| Group | Metadata definition | Samples |\n|---|---|---:|\n| TCGA colon primary tumors (COAD-like) | `_study=TCGA`, `_primary_site=Colon`, `_sample_type=Primary Tumor`, `detailed_category=Colon Adenocarcinoma` | 288 |\n| TCGA rectum primary tumors (READ-like) | `_study=TCGA`, `_primary_site=Rectum`, `_sample_type=Primary Tumor`, `detailed_category=Rectum Adenocarcinoma` | 92 |\n| TCGA colon solid-tissue normals | `_study=TCGA`, site Colon, `_sample_type=Solid Tissue Normal` | 41 |\n| TCGA rectum solid-tissue normals | `_study=TCGA`, site Rectum, `_sample_type=Solid Tissue Normal` | 10 |\n| GTEx colon normal | `_study=GTEX`, `_primary_site=Colon`, `_sample_type=Normal Tissue` | 308 |\n| Other GTEx normal tissues | `_study=GTEX`, `_sample_type=Normal Tissue`, site not Colon | 7,121 |\n\nGTEx colon samples are further annotated as sigmoid (141) or transverse (167). The metadata also distinguishes a small number of colorectal metastatic or recurrent tumor samples, so those can be kept separate from primary tumors.\n\nTCGA “Solid Tissue Normal” samples are distinguishable from tumor samples, but the metadata does not confirm that each normal sample is an adjacent, patient-matched specimen. The category dataset, **`TCGA_GTEX_category.txt`**, provides useful broad tissue/disease labels, but its own metadata says TCGA solid-tissue normals are excluded; use the phenotype dataset to classify normals.\n\nThe matrix contains **19,131 samples total**, including 734 TARGET samples. Filter on `_study` as well as tissue and sample type to keep the analysis to TCGA and GTEx.\n\n## Targeted extraction and recommendation\n\nA targeted Xena API query for the CDH17 Ensembl feature returned values for five specified samples, and the phenotype data were retrievable in sample chunks. The API supports requesting selected features and samples, so the full matrix is not required for a one-gene extraction. The tested endpoint was `https://toil.xenahubs.net/data/`; the `xenaPython` client documents the same style of targeted query.\n\n**Recommended acquisition method:** use the Xena API from CoCalc to retrieve `ENSG00000079112.9` and the selected phenotype fields, matching by `sampleID`. Fetch in chunks if needed. This is feasible with the environment’s existing `requests` package and avoids the 1.32 GB matrix download.\n\n## Limitations\n\nToil’s common processing supports comparison across studies, but the groups still come from different sources: GTEx normal tissues and TCGA tumors/solid-tissue normals. The hub metadata does not document batch correction, and the GTEx-versus-TCGA comparison may retain source or collection effects. Comparing TCGA tumors with TCGA solid-tissue normals keeps the source more consistent; treat GTEx comparisons as a separate reference.\n\nThe Toil dataset version is dated 2016-09-03. The metadata identifies the annotation version and transformation, but does not give enough detail here to confirm every upstream pipeline or GTEx release version.\n\n## Verified source links\n\n- [Xena dataset record: `TcgaTargetGtex_rsem_gene_tpm`](https://xenabrowser.net/datapages/?dataset=TcgaTargetGtex_rsem_gene_tpm&host=https%3A%2F%2Ftoil.xenahubs.net)\n- [Compressed expression matrix endpoint](https://toil.xenahubs.net/download/TcgaTargetGtex_rsem_gene_tpm.gz)\n- [Xena dataset record: `TcgaTargetGTEX_phenotype.txt`](https://xenabrowser.net/datapages/?dataset=TcgaTargetGTEX_phenotype.txt&host=https%3A%2F%2Ftoil.xenahubs.net)\n- [Compressed phenotype metadata endpoint](https://toil.xenahubs.net/download/TcgaTargetGTEX_phenotype.txt.gz) — verified size: **135,753 bytes**\n- [Xena dataset record: `TCGA_GTEX_category.txt`](https://xenabrowser.net/datapages/?dataset=TCGA_GTEX_category.txt&host=https%3A%2F%2Ftoil.xenahubs.net)\n- [Xena hub API documentation and examples](https://github.com/ucscXena/xenaPython)\n- [Ensembl lookup for the CDH17 gene ID](https://rest.ensembl.org/lookup/id/ENSG00000079112?content-type=application/json)\n\nNo analysis, figures, pipeline, or project files were created. I stopped at the feasibility review.","date":"2026-11-25T17:09:38.795Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/CDH17 Final Project.chat","acp_log_key":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e:bacf7ccf-49d0-4cba-8c7e-21162a69b008","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e.bacf7ccf-49d0-4cba-8c7e-21162a69b008","acp_started_at_ms":1795626043360,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis","acp_account_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"bacf7ccf-49d0-4cba-8c7e-21162a69b008","thread_id":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e","parent_message_id":"76e5168a-713e-4e75-ae75-ec48f1b3ca3f","acp_thread_id":"01a213a4-fe33-7541-be04-ae44f8966e75","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":82256,"cached_input_tokens":78320,"output_tokens":10029,"reasoning_output_tokens":8646,"total_tokens":92285,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-25T17:16:14.091Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"## Completed\n\nCreated and published the acquisition script and five requested data and QC files, plus the raw all-sample intermediate. No full expression matrix was downloaded, and no statistical comparisons or figures were made.\n\n| File | Rows × columns | Size |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| [Acquisition script](</home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/scripts/01_download_cdh17.py>) | — | 34 KB |\n| [Annotated dataset](</home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/data/cdh17_expression_annotated.csv>) | 7,860 × 14 | 1,318,722 bytes |\n| [Raw all-sample intermediate](</home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/data/cdh17_expression_raw_all_samples.csv>) | 19,131 × 13 | 2,949,793 bytes |\n| [QC summary](</home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/results/data_qc_summary.csv>) | 52 metrics | 3,388 bytes |\n| [QC report](</home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/results/data_qc_report.md>) | — | 4,294 bytes |\n| [Data provenance](</home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/data/data_provenance.md>) | — | 4,841 bytes |\n\n## QC findings\n\nThe script retrieved only CDH17 feature `ENSG00000079112.9` and the specified phenotype fields from the Toil Xena API. It preserved the reported `log2(TPM + 0.001)` values.\n\nAll six group counts matched the feasibility findings: 288 colon tumors, 92 rectum tumors, 41 colon normals, 10 rectum normals, 308 GTEx colon normals, and 7,121 other GTEx normal tissues. The GTEx colon labels include 167 transverse and 141 sigmoid samples.\n\nAll 19,131 expression and phenotype sample IDs joined by `sampleID`; there were no duplicate IDs, unmatched rows, missing expression values, or nonnumeric expression values. The raw intermediate retains excluded samples, including 734 TARGET samples, 3 noneligible colorectal TCGA samples, 10,101 other TCGA samples, and 433 GTEx cell-line samples.\n\nFour GTEx normal samples had a blank broad site field but identifiable detailed tissue labels, so they were retained among other GTEx normals. Missing phenotype fields remain blank and are counted in the QC summary. TCGA normals are not assumed to be paired with tumors.\n\nTwo consecutive retrievals produced identical hashes for all five generated data and report files. No blockers were found. The provenance document records the Xena URLs and reference file sizes; the full matrix was not downloaded.","date":"2026-11-25T17:23:05.985Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/CDH17 Final Project.chat","acp_log_key":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e:0e69971b-af78-41ed-ae16-50ed49b7e125","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e.0e69971b-af78-41ed-ae16-50ed49b7e125","acp_started_at_ms":1795626975194,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis","acp_account_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"0e69971b-af78-41ed-ae16-50ed49b7e125","thread_id":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e","parent_message_id":"3c3c18e0-6172-4645-8373-c483a9682334","acp_thread_id":"01a213a4-fe33-7541-be04-ae44f8966e75","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":54930,"cached_input_tokens":54023,"output_tokens":1312,"reasoning_output_tokens":737,"total_tokens":56242,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-25T17:37:24.832Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"## Completed\n\nThe notebook executed successfully from a clean kernel: all 8 code cells completed with **zero errors**. I selected the installed Python 3 (Sage) kernel; no packages were installed. The source CSV remains unchanged.\n\n- [EDA notebook](/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/notebooks/02_CDH17_EDA.ipynb) — 420,591 bytes\n- [Descriptive statistics CSV](/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/results/eda_summary.csv) — 902 bytes\n- [Figure A: TCGA colorectal distributions](/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/figures/figure_A_tcga_colorectal_distributions.png) — 181,131 bytes, 2719 × 1700\n- [Figure B: TCGA tumors and GTEx colon](/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/figures/figure_B_tcga_tumors_vs_gtex_colon.png) — 203,716 bytes, 2299 × 1700\n- [Figure C: GTEx normal tissues](/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/figures/figure_C_gtex_normal_tissues.png) — 623,830 bytes, 3018 × 4014\n\nThe input had **7,860 rows and 14 columns**, with six groups matching the prior feasibility counts. Expression values remain on the reported $log_2(TPM + 0.001)$ scale.\n\n| Group | n | Median |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| TCGA colon primary tumors | 288 | 7.4535 |\n| TCGA rectum primary tumors | 92 | 7.6750 |\n| TCGA colon solid-tissue normals | 41 | 8.2430 |\n| TCGA rectum solid-tissue normals | 10 | 7.9195 |\n| GTEx normal colon | 308 | 1.4200 |\n| Other GTEx normal tissues | 7,121 | -4.2930 |\n\n## QC observations\n\nThere were **no duplicate sample IDs, missing expression values, nonnumeric expression values, or anatomical-label mismatches**. Four GTEx records lack `_primary_site`; their detailed tissue labels were retained. The 308 GTEx colon samples comprise 167 transverse and 141 sigmoid samples. Other GTEx tissues retain 49 detailed labels.\n\nThe observed minimum, -9.966, is at the transformation’s theoretical floor, approximately $log_2(0.001)=-9.965784$. **1,447 samples** are at that minimum, all in “Other GTEx normal tissues”; that group’s most common value accounts for 20.32% of its samples. Descriptive Tukey-fence flags were also recorded in the notebook and are not treated as evidence of erroneous measurements.\n\nThe figures show the expected broad spread in GTEx colon and the floor concentration among other GTEx tissues. TCGA and GTEx remain distinct data sources, with no batch correction applied. No hypothesis tests or biological or clinical conclusions were made. The notebook documents how to rerun it from the project directory or with `CDH17_PROJECT_ROOT` set.","date":"2026-11-25T17:42:00.340Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/CDH17 Final Project.chat","acp_log_key":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e:b518f6a5-5ebe-492c-b4f4-bbe42c8083dd","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e.b518f6a5-5ebe-492c-b4f4-bbe42c8083dd","acp_started_at_ms":1795628245627,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis","acp_account_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"b518f6a5-5ebe-492c-b4f4-bbe42c8083dd","thread_id":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e","parent_message_id":"72fef28e-8289-45e6-9281-0f4d975985fa","acp_thread_id":"01a213a4-fe33-7541-be04-ae44f8966e75","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":86934,"cached_input_tokens":86153,"output_tokens":1193,"reasoning_output_tokens":516,"total_tokens":88127,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-25T17:52:29.574Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"The independent audit is complete in [expression_discrepancy_audit.md](/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/results/expression_discrepancy_audit.md). It is also published in the project chat as a file reference.\n\nAll six medians matched the saved EDA values. The 7,860 rows have unique sample IDs, successful joins, and no missing or nonnumeric expression values. Group reconstruction matched all six labels; four GTEx rows with missing broad tissue labels were classified using their detailed tissue labels.\n\nThe audit documents the 6.823-unit TCGA colon-normal versus pooled GTEx-colon median gap and the substantial GTEx subsite split: sigmoid median −1.056 ($n=141$), transverse median 6.908 ($n=167$). It also reports floor-equivalent proportions and descriptive TCGA outlier flags without removing observations.\n\nNo hypothesis tests or figures were produced, and the source CSVs, acquisition script, notebook, and existing figures were left unchanged. TCGA colon subsite and per-sample collection or batch details remain unavailable, limiting interpretation of the cross-source difference.","date":"2026-11-25T17:57:39.270Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/CDH17 Final Project.chat","acp_log_key":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e:e9ab086d-dd04-4468-84b2-67741bc209b0","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e.e9ab086d-dd04-4468-84b2-67741bc209b0","acp_started_at_ms":1795629149873,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis","acp_account_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"e9ab086d-dd04-4468-84b2-67741bc209b0","thread_id":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e","parent_message_id":"37ef5040-a967-46d6-ac2b-8191ecf76505","acp_thread_id":"01a213a4-fe33-7541-be04-ae44f8966e75","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":57271,"cached_input_tokens":56005,"output_tokens":457,"reasoning_output_tokens":219,"total_tokens":57728,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-25T18:29:15.092Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"Implemented and executed the three prespecified unpaired Mann–Whitney U comparisons using the original `log2(TPM + 0.001)` values. The script validated the selected samples against the original phenotype annotations. Rerunning it from outside the project directory also succeeded.\n\n| Comparison (group 1 vs group 2) | n | Medians | Median difference | Rank-biserial correlation | Two-sided p-value | Holm-adjusted p-value* |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| TCGA colon tumor vs normal | 288 vs 41 | 7.4535 vs 8.2430 | −0.7895 | −0.5812 | 1.73 × 10⁻⁹ | 3.47 × 10⁻⁹ |\n| TCGA rectum tumor vs normal | 92 vs 10 | 7.6750 vs 7.9195 | −0.2445 | −0.2293 | 0.2374 | 0.2374 |\n| GTEx sigmoid vs transverse colon | 141 vs 167 | −1.0560 vs 6.9080 | −7.9640 | −0.7317 | 1.89 × 10⁻²⁸ | — |\n\nNegative differences and effect sizes indicate lower expression ranks in the first group. The rectum comparison was not statistically significant; with only 10 rectum normal samples, this is not evidence of equivalence. The GTEx subsite comparison is exploratory and was not included in the primary-test adjustment.\n\nCreated and published the requested files:\n\n- [Analysis script](</home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/scripts/03_statistical_analysis.py>)\n- [Statistical summary CSV](</home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/results/statistical_summary.csv>)\n- [Methods and results notes](</home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/results/statistical_analysis_notes.md>)\n- [Figure D](</home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/figures/figure_D_tcga_statistical_comparisons.png>)\n\n\\*Holm adjustment applied to the two primary TCGA comparisons only.","date":"2026-11-25T18:30:50.810Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/CDH17 Final Project.chat","acp_log_key":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e:9cfd8fd4-50b5-4f5d-ac0e-db8df6656ac2","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e.9cfd8fd4-50b5-4f5d-ac0e-db8df6656ac2","acp_started_at_ms":1795631356198,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis","acp_account_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"9cfd8fd4-50b5-4f5d-ac0e-db8df6656ac2","thread_id":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e","parent_message_id":"13609ed9-101b-4fc2-ab18-07029aa9887a","acp_thread_id":"01a213a4-fe33-7541-be04-ae44f8966e75","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":35422,"cached_input_tokens":31433,"output_tokens":637,"reasoning_output_tokens":162,"total_tokens":36059,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-25T19:12:38.984Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"## Prepared files\n\nCreated the GitHub preparation documents:\n\n- [README.md](/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/README.md)\n- [requirements.txt](/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/requirements.txt)\n- [.gitignore](/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/.gitignore)\n- [REPRODUCIBILITY.md](/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/REPRODUCIBILITY.md)\n- [AI implementation plan](/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/ai_documentation/AI_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md)\n\nThe docs were published as CoCalc file references for review. No GitHub repository was created and nothing was pushed.\n\n## Proposed repository structure\n\n```text\nCDH17_Analysis/\n├── .gitignore\n├── README.md\n├── REPRODUCIBILITY.md\n├── requirements.txt\n├── ai_documentation/\n│   └── AI_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n├── data/\n│   ├── cdh17_expression_annotated.csv\n│   └── data_provenance.md\n├── figures/\n│   ├── figure_A_tcga_colorectal_distributions.png\n│   ├── figure_B_tcga_tumors_vs_gtex_colon.png\n│   ├── figure_C_gtex_normal_tissues.png\n│   └── figure_D_tcga_statistical_comparisons.png\n├── notebooks/\n│   └── 02_CDH17_EDA.ipynb\n├── results/\n│   ├── data_qc_report.md\n│   ├── data_qc_summary.csv\n│   ├── eda_summary.csv\n│   ├── expression_discrepancy_audit.md\n│   ├── statistical_analysis_notes.md\n│   └── statistical_summary.csv\n└── scripts/\n    ├── 01_download_cdh17.py\n    └── 03_statistical_analysis.py\n```\n\nThe proposed repository includes the compact annotated dataset and its provenance. The 2.95 MB `data/cdh17_expression_raw_all_samples.csv` intermediate and `CDH17 Final Project.chat` should remain CoCalc-only; `.gitignore` excludes them. The annotated CSV is not ignored.\n\n## Audit and reproducibility\n\nBoth analysis scripts resolve paths from the project root. The notebook locates the root from its current directory or `CDH17_PROJECT_ROOT`. I found no dependencies on local files outside the project and no likely hardcoded credentials or tokens. `requirements.txt` pins the installed, tested package versions, including the notebook execution dependencies.\n\nA non-destructive end-to-end check ran in a temporary directory:\n\n- Targeted Xena retrieval reproduced the saved annotated dataset exactly: **7,860 rows × 14 columns**.\n- EDA summary and statistical summary matched the saved CSVs exactly; statistical notes also matched.\n- Figures C and D were pixel-identical.\n- Figures A and B differed slightly at the pixel level because their point jitter is unseeded. Their underlying data and summaries reproduced; this limitation is recorded in the reproducibility guide. The validated project figures were left unchanged.\n\nNo blocking data or code issue surfaced. For bit-for-bit figure reproducibility, seed or replace the jitter and review any regenerated Figures A and B before treating them as final. The local AI documentation folder had no existing records, and the course’s AI-use policy or template was not available here; the new outline describes the workflow and review checkpoints without inventing prompts or chat history. If the course requires additional AI records, those requirements still need to be checked.\n\nThe existing acquisition and statistical scripts received documentation-only path instruction edits; the statistical notes’ reproduction command was also made relative. No scientific results or Figures A–D were changed.","date":"2026-11-25T19:16:21.018Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/CDH17 Final Project.chat","acp_log_key":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e:289cd615-1ac6-43b3-a562-20db05886f1e","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e.289cd615-1ac6-43b3-a562-20db05886f1e","acp_started_at_ms":1795633960122,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/P00_Final_Pr