{"sender_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","content":"Continue the BIOM5350 CDH17 Final Project in /home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/.\n\nPhase 4 EDA has been completed successfully. Before formal statistical testing, we need to investigate several unexpected findings.\n\nObserved medians, log2(TPM + 0.001):\nTCGA colon tumor: 7.4535\nTCGA colon normal: 8.2430\nTCGA rectum tumor: 7.6750\nTCGA rectum normal: 7.9195\nGTEx colon normal: 1.4200\nOther GTEx normal tissues: -4.2930\n\nTASK: Perform an independent audit of these findings. Do NOT modify existing source data or EDA figures.\n\n1. Recalculate the six medians independently from the saved annotated CSV and verify the values.\n2. Verify that all comparisons use the same gene identifier, expression transformation and Xena expression dataset.\n3. Recheck the TCGA and GTEx sample classifications using the preserved original phenotype columns.\n4. For GTEx colon, separately examine sigmoid and transverse colon. Report counts, medians, quartiles, and zero/floor proportions.\n5. For TCGA colon and rectum, examine tumor and normal distributions, including sample counts, quartiles, floor proportions and any unusual outliers.\n6. Summarize the ten highest-expressing GTEx normal tissue categories, including counts and median expression. Do not combine biologically distinct organs under misleading labels.\n7. Investigate whether the large TCGA-versus-GTEx normal-colon difference could reflect differences in collection, tissue composition, or batch/source effects. Distinguish documented facts from hypotheses; do not assume a specific cause without evidence.\n8. Propose a defensible statistical analysis plan, prioritizing within-TCGA comparisons and treating cross-source comparisons as exploratory.\n9. Write results/expression_discrepancy_audit.md. Include numerical evidence, unresolved limitations, and recommended next steps.\n\nDo not perform formal hypothesis testing yet.\nDo not change the acquisition script, source CSVs, or Phase 4 notebook.\nDo not create additional figures unless needed to verify a suspected labeling or data error.\nStop after reporting the audit findings and proposed analysis plan for review.","date":"2026-11-25T17:52:29.014Z"}],"date":"2026-11-25T17:52:29.014Z","message_id":"37ef5040-a967-46d6-ac2b-8191ecf76505","thread_id":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e","parent_message_id":"b518f6a5-5ebe-492c-b4f4-bbe42c8083dd","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}
{"sender_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","content":"Continue the BIOM5350 CDH17 Final Project.\n\nLOCAL PROJECT:\n/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/\n\nGITHUB REPOSITORY:\ngit@github.com:wumianyang233/BIOM5350-CDH17-Analysis.git\n\nThe GitHub repository already exists and is empty. The project files were prepared and audited in the previous step.\n\nTASK: Publish the reviewed project to GitHub via SSH.\n\n1. Verify SSH authentication using ssh -T git@github.com.\n2. Inspect the project directory and .gitignore before initializing Git.\n3. Ensure the CoCalc AI chat file, credentials, tokens, caches, temporary outputs, and unnecessary large intermediate data are excluded.\n4. Check exactly which files will be tracked. Include the analysis scripts, EDA notebook, essential small dataset, reproducibility documentation, README, requirements, results, figures, and approved AI implementation-plan document.\n5. Do not include the raw all-sample intermediate CSV or temporary reproducibility test files.\n6. Initialize a Git repository in the local project directory if one does not already exist.\n7. Set the branch name to main and add the GitHub repository as origin using the SSH URL above.\n8. Stage only the reviewed files and show git status before committing.\n9. Commit with the message: \"Add reproducible CDH17 expression analysis pipeline\".\n10. Push the main branch to origin.\n11. Verify the remote branch and report the commit hash, tracked file count, and final git status.\n12. Confirm that README.md, scripts, notebook, figures, results, and documentation are visible in the remote repository.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Do not modify the scientific data or analysis results.\n- Do not overwrite or force-push any remote history.\n- Do not commit the CoCalc chat transcript.\n- Do not commit any private credentials.\n- Do not change the project folder location.\n- Stop and report any authentication errors, unexpected existing Git history, or unreviewed files instead of making potentially destructive changes.\n- After publishing, provide a concise summary of the files uploaded and verification results.","date":"2026-11-25T19:28:09.467Z"}],"date":"2026-11-25T19:28:09.467Z","message_id":"e2a30b16-880d-42db-89bc-85edeefdaf94","thread_id":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e","parent_message_id":"289cd615-1ac6-43b3-a562-20db05886f1e","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}
{"sender_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","content":"Continue the BIOM5350 CDH17 Final Project.\n\nPROJECT ROOT:\n/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/\n\nPhase 3 data acquisition and QC have been completed. The cleaned analysis dataset contains 7,860 samples across six groups.\n\nTASK: Create and execute a reproducible exploratory data analysis (EDA) notebook. Do not perform formal hypothesis testing yet.\n\n1. Read data/cdh17_expression_annotated.csv. First inspect and validate the actual column names, types, group labels, expression scale, and row counts. Do not assume column names without checking.\n\n2. Create notebooks/02_CDH17_EDA.ipynb, with clear Markdown explanations and code cells organized from beginning to end. If the notebook cannot execute in the current environment, report that limitation and create a corresponding standalone Python script, without installing packages yet.\n\n3. Calculate descriptive statistics for each of the six analysis groups:\n   - Sample count\n   - Mean and median expression\n   - Standard deviation\n   - 25th and 75th percentiles\n   - Minimum and maximum\n   - Missingness\n\n4. Generate three exploratory visualizations:\n   Figure A: CDH17 expression distributions for TCGA colon tumors, rectum tumors, colon normals, and rectum normals.\n   Figure B: TCGA colorectal tumors versus GTEx normal colon, clearly labeling the different data sources.\n   Figure C: CDH17 expression across GTEx normal tissues, using meaningful detailed anatomical labels and a readable ordering.\n\n5. Use the expression values in their original reported scale, log2(TPM + 0.001). Do not incorrectly relabel them as log2(TPM + 1).\n\n6. Save publication-readable PNG figures to figures/ and descriptive statistics to results/eda_summary.csv. Use descriptive titles, axes, sample counts where helpful, and consistent styling.\n\n7. Check for extreme values, unusually concentrated distributions, potential floor effects, and tissue-label inconsistencies. Report observations without making unsupported biological conclusions.\n\n8. Make the notebook rerunnable from the project directory, with relative paths or a clearly documented project-root setting. Avoid hardcoded assumptions about the current working directory.\n\n9. Execute and verify each analysis step. Report created file paths, group medians, any surprising results, notebook execution status, and limitations.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Do not run t-tests, Wilcoxon tests, ANOVA, or other inferential statistical tests yet.\n- Do not perform batch correction.\n- Do not modify the Phase 3 acquisition script or source CSV files.\n- Do not create or push a GitHub repository yet.\n- Do not interpret RNA expression as proof of protein abundance, ADC efficacy, or clinical safety.\n- Stop after reporting the EDA outputs for review.","date":"2026-11-25T17:37:24.080Z"}],"date":"2026-11-25T17:37:24.080Z","message_id":"72fef28e-8289-45e6-9281-0f4d975985fa","thread_id":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e","parent_message_id":"0e69971b-af78-41ed-ae16-50ed49b7e125","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}
{"sender_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","content":"Continue the BIOM5350 CDH17 Final Project.\n\nPROJECT ROOT:\n/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/\n\nSOURCE CHAT:\nCDH17 Final Project.chat\n\nDESTINATION:\nai_documentation/\n\nTASK:\nExport the complete existing CoCalc AI conversation history into the ai_documentation folder for the course's AI-use documentation requirement.\n\n1. Locate the original \"CDH17 Final Project.chat\" file in the project root.\n2. Preserve the original chat file in its current location. Do not delete, overwrite, or move it.\n3. Export the complete conversation into:\n   ai_documentation/AI_CHAT_HISTORY.md\n4. Include all available user prompts and AI responses in chronological order, preserving their wording and technical details as faithfully as possible.\n5. Preserve timestamps if available. Clearly identify user and AI messages.\n6. Do not summarize, paraphrase, fabricate, or omit conversation content. If the complete history cannot be exported, explicitly report the limitation rather than claiming a complete export.\n7. If CoCalc does not support direct Markdown export, investigate its supported chat export functionality and use a safe, non-destructive method. Do not attempt to parse undocumented internal binary formats.\n8. Verify that the exported file is readable and contains the conversation from the earliest available message through the latest available message.\n9. Do not include unrelated ChatGPT conversations or invent missing messages.\n10. Check the exported content for credentials, API keys, or other private secrets. If any are present, stop and report their location without publishing them.\n\nAfter verification:\n11. Stage only ai_documentation/AI_CHAT_HISTORY.md and any necessary updates to the existing AI implementation documentation.\n12. Commit with the message \"Add CoCalc AI conversation history\".\n13. Push to the existing GitHub repository:\ngit@github.com:wumianyang233/BIOM5350-CDH17-Analysis.git\n14. Verify that the Markdown chat history is readable on GitHub.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Do not modify analysis scripts, datasets, notebooks, figures, statistical results, or other validated scientific files.\n- Do not change the original .chat file.\n- Do not force-push.\n- Do not include any external ChatGPT conversations.\n- If complete export is not technically possible, stop and explain the available alternatives before committing.\n\nFinally, report the exported filename, message count if available, completeness check, Git commit hash, and GitHub publication status.","date":"2026-11-25T19:36:42.743Z"}],"date":"2026-11-25T19:36:42.743Z","message_id":"00267bff-87d9-4b8d-9fd5-d41d4729d420","thread_id":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e","parent_message_id":"cedb6605-8971-46ed-a1ce-329a8f4f0d85","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}
{"sender_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","content":"Continue the BIOM5350 CDH17 Final Project.\n\nPROJECT ROOT:\n/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/\n\nThe biological analysis is now complete. Data acquisition, QC, EDA, statistical testing, and Figures A-D have been reviewed.\n\nWe are preparing the project for submission to a public GitHub repository. This is a bioinformatics programming course final project, so keep the repository simple, clean, and reproducible.\n\nTASK: Prepare and audit the existing project files for GitHub. Do NOT upload or push anything yet.\n\n1. Inspect the current project directory and list all existing files with their sizes.\n\n2. Create a clear README.md containing:\n   - Project title and short biological research question\n   - Dataset sources (UCSC Xena TCGA/GTEx Toil)\n   - CDH17 gene identifier\n   - Brief project structure\n   - Python environment and required packages\n   - Exact commands to reproduce data acquisition, EDA, and statistical analysis\n   - Summary of the three statistical comparisons\n   - Explanation of the log2(TPM + 0.001) expression scale\n   - Main limitations, especially TCGA/GTEx source differences and RNA-versus-protein interpretation\n\n3. Create requirements.txt with only the packages actually required by the project's Python code. Verify that the versions or version ranges are appropriate for reproducibility.\n\n4. Create .gitignore to exclude:\n   - Python caches and temporary files\n   - Jupyter checkpoints\n   - CoCalc-specific temporary files\n   - Credentials, secrets, and environment files\n   - Large raw data files not needed in GitHub\n   Do not automatically exclude small essential reproducibility files.\n\n5. Review the existing acquisition script, EDA notebook, and statistical analysis script:\n   - Ensure all input/output paths are documented and reproducible.\n   - Verify that they do not depend on files outside the project except explicitly documented public sources.\n   - Ensure there are no hardcoded personal credentials or private tokens.\n   - Identify any execution-order problems.\n\n6. Create a short reproducibility guide named REPRODUCIBILITY.md. Include the exact order and commands needed to regenerate the dataset, descriptive statistics, statistical results, and figures.\n\n7. Inspect the ai_documentation/ folder and identify documentation needed to satisfy the course's AI-use requirements. Create a factual implementation-plan outline describing the actual workflow and human review checkpoints. Do not fabricate prompts, chat history, or verification steps. Do not overwrite existing AI records.\n\n8. Run a non-destructive reproducibility check where feasible. Do not delete, overwrite, or regenerate validated outputs merely for testing. Use a temporary test directory if necessary and compare generated results with the saved outputs.\n\n9. Produce a final report showing:\n   - Complete proposed GitHub file structure\n   - Files ready for publication\n   - Files that should remain only on CoCalc\n   - Missing documentation or dependencies\n   - Reproducibility check results\n   - Any problems that must be fixed before publishing\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Do not create a GitHub repository yet.\n- Do not run git init, git push, or upload files.\n- Do not modify validated scientific results or Figures A-D.\n- Do not delete or move the original project files.\n- Do not create a new biological analysis.\n- Keep the deliverables proportional to a normal bioinformatics programming course final project.\n- Stop after preparing the files and reporting the results for review.","date":"2026-11-25T19:12:38.121Z"}],"date":"2026-11-25T19:12:38.121Z","message_id":"74d77a4f-1025-43e1-9934-cd432e419589","thread_id":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e","parent_message_id":"9cfd8fd4-50b5-4f5d-ac0e-db8df6656ac2","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}
{"sender_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","content":"Continue the BIOM5350 CDH17 Final Project.\n\nPROJECT ROOT:\n/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/\n\nThe previous attempt to export the complete chat as Markdown was unsuccessful.\n\nNEW TASK:\nPreserve and publish the original native CoCalc chat file instead.\n\n1. Locate the original file:\n   CDH17 Final Project.chat\n2. Copy it without modifying the original into:\n   ai_documentation/CDH17 Final Project.chat\n3. Verify that the copied file is byte-identical to the original using SHA-256 hashes.\n4. Check the file size and inspect for sensitive credentials or tokens using supported safe methods. Do not invent transcript content or alter the native chat format.\n5. Check whether .gitignore excludes .chat files.\n6. If the file is safe to publish, stage only the copied chat file, using git add -f for that specific file if necessary.\n7. Commit with the message:\n   Add original CoCalc AI chat record\n8. Push to the existing GitHub main branch without force.\n9. Verify that the file appears under ai_documentation/ on GitHub.\n\nDo not modify the original chat, research data, scripts, notebooks, figures, results, or existing documentation.\n\nDo not claim that GitHub can render the native chat format. Report whether the file is readable outside CoCalc and whether an additional human-readable export is still necessary.\n\nIf the file cannot be safely inspected, copied, or published, stop and explain the problem without committing.\n\nReport the file size, checksum comparison, commit hash, and publication status.","date":"2026-11-25T19:48:02.033Z"}],"date":"2026-11-25T19:48:02.033Z","message_id":"19352311-8871-43dd-b2ff-090159dd08f8","thread_id":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e","parent_message_id":"d98ab540-19fe-46a0-9c3e-6cba38ca7297","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}
{"sender_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","content":"Continue the BIOM5350 CDH17 Final Project.\n\nProject root:\n/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/\n\nThe data acquisition, QC, EDA, and independent expression audit are complete. We now need a small, focused statistical analysis suitable for a bioinformatics programming course final project.\n\nTASK: Perform exactly three prespecified, unpaired comparisons:\n\n1. TCGA colon primary tumors vs TCGA colon solid-tissue normals (primary).\n2. TCGA rectum primary tumors vs TCGA rectum solid-tissue normals (primary).\n3. GTEx sigmoid colon vs GTEx transverse colon normals (secondary, exploratory).\n\nBefore analysis, inspect the actual dataset column names and verify sample selection using the original annotations. Ensure the three comparisons use the correct groups and do not treat samples as patient-matched pairs.\n\nUse:\n- Two-sided Mann–Whitney U tests.\n- Median expression difference (first group minus second) on the original log2(TPM + 0.001) scale.\n- An interpretable nonparametric effect size such as rank-biserial correlation, with the direction clearly defined.\n- Holm multiple-testing adjustment for the two primary TCGA tests only. Keep the GTEx exploratory test separate.\n- Report actual group sizes and p-values. Avoid interpreting nonsignificant results as evidence of equivalence.\n\nImplementation:\n1. Create scripts/03_statistical_analysis.py as a reproducible, rerunnable script.\n2. Save results/statistical_summary.csv containing all three comparisons, sample sizes, group medians, median differences, effect sizes, unadjusted p-values, and adjusted p-values where applicable.\n3. Create results/statistical_analysis_notes.md with a short explanation of the methods, observed results, limitations, and appropriate interpretation.\n4. Create one clear figure showing the two within-TCGA comparisons, with accurate labels and sample sizes. Save it in figures/ as figure_D_tcga_statistical_comparisons.png. Avoid adding significance stars without reporting the actual p-values.\n5. Keep the existing dataset, acquisition script, EDA notebook, and Figures A–C unchanged.\n6. Execute and verify the new script. Report the actual numerical results and file paths.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nThis is a small bioinformatics course final project, not a clinical research paper. Keep the analysis straightforward and reproducible.\nDo not add machine learning, survival analysis, differential expression across the whole transcriptome, batch correction, or additional datasets.\nDo not make conclusions about ADC safety or clinical efficacy based on RNA expression alone.\nStop after completing the statistical analysis and reporting the results for review.","date":"2026-11-25T18:29:14.183Z"}],"date":"2026-11-25T18:29:14.183Z","message_id":"13609ed9-101b-4fc2-ab18-07029aa9887a","thread_id":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e","parent_message_id":"e9ab086d-dd04-4468-84b2-67741bc209b0","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}
{"sender_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","content":"Continue the BIOM5350 CDH17 project from the verified UCSC Xena feasibility findings in this chat.\n\nPROJECT ROOT:\n/home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/\n\nTASK: Implement and execute ONLY a reproducible data acquisition and initial quality-control step. Do not begin statistical comparisons or figures yet.\n\nUse the verified Toil Xena expression dataset TcgaTargetGtex_rsem_gene_tpm and matching TcgaTargetGTEX_phenotype.txt. The CDH17 feature is ENSG00000079112.9, with reported log2(TPM + 0.001) expression values.\n\n1. Create scripts/01_download_cdh17.py that requests only the CDH17 gene expression values and the matching sample annotations via the verified Xena API. Do not download the full expression matrix. Use requests with timeouts, basic retry handling, and clear errors. Make the script safely rerunnable.\n\n2. Join values and phenotype annotations explicitly by sampleID, not by relying on order. Check for duplicate IDs, missing values, failed joins, nonnumeric expression values, and inconsistent sample counts.\n\n3. Define separate groups using the verified phenotype labels:\n   - TCGA colon primary tumors\n   - TCGA rectum primary tumors\n   - TCGA colon solid-tissue normals\n   - TCGA rectum solid-tissue normals\n   - GTEx normal colon (retain sigmoid/transverse labels if available)\n   - Other GTEx normal tissues (retain detailed anatomical tissue labels)\n   Exclude TARGET, metastatic/recurrent tumors, and ambiguous or unclassified samples from the main analysis dataset. Do not assume TCGA normals are paired with tumors.\n\n4. Preserve both raw phenotype fields and a clean analysis_group field. Keep the reported transformed expression values unchanged. Do not convert log2(TPM + 0.001) to log2(TPM + 1). Do not apply batch correction or other normalization.\n\n5. Save:\n   data/cdh17_expression_annotated.csv\n   results/data_qc_summary.csv\n   results/data_qc_report.md\n   data/data_provenance.md\n   scripts/01_download_cdh17.py\n\n6. In the provenance document, include the exact Xena hub URL, dataset IDs, gene identifier, expression scale, access date, sample annotations, and reproducible retrieval instructions. In the QC report, include row counts for all groups, missingness, duplicate checks, join success, exclusion counts, and any unexpected results.\n\n7. Verify the script can successfully reproduce the saved dataset. Report the actual number of rows and columns, file sizes, and QC findings. Compare group counts with the earlier feasibility findings, and explain any differences rather than forcing the expected values.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Keep the original sample-level data, even for excluded categories, if feasible, in a separate raw/intermediate file.\n- Do not overwrite the existing CoCalc chat or unrelated files.\n- Do not download the full expression matrix.\n- Do not perform hypothesis testing, calculate group differences, interpret CDH17 biology, or create figures yet.\n- Do not silently impute missing values or discard questionable data.\n- Stop and report the completed files, QC outcomes, and any blockers for human review.","date":"2026-11-25T17:16:13.258Z"}],"date":"2026-11-25T17:16:13.258Z","message_id":"3c3c18e0-6172-4645-8373-c483a9682334","thread_id":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e","parent_message_id":"bacf7ccf-49d0-4cba-8c7e-21162a69b008","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}
{"sender_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","content":"We are starting the BIOM5350 Fall 2026 Final Project.\n\nProject: CDH17 Expression and Tissue Selectivity in Colorectal Cancer.\n\nOur goal is to develop a reproducible Python analysis pipeline using publicly available TCGA and GTEx RNA-seq data to compare CDH17 expression in colorectal tumors and normal tissues.\n\nFor now, please complete ONLY the following tasks:\n\n1. Confirm that the project directory exists:\n   /home/user/P00_Final_Project/CDH17_Analysis/\n\n2. Create these subdirectories inside it:\n   data/\n   notebooks/\n   scripts/\n   results/\n   figures/\n   ai_documentation/\n\n3. Check the installed Python version and availability of:\n   pandas, numpy, scipy, matplotlib, seaborn, requests, and jupyter.\n\n4. Check whether the workspace can access publicly available internet resources. Use a small, non-destructive connectivity test. Do not download datasets.\n\n5. Report the directory structure, package versions, available disk space, and any limitations.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Do not overwrite, rename, or delete existing files.\n- Do not install packages yet.\n- Do not download datasets yet.\n- Do not write the analysis pipeline yet.\n- Stop after reporting your findings and wait for further instructions.","date":"2026-11-25T16:58:25.315Z"}],"date":"2026-11-25T16:58:25.315Z","message_id":"9156dfb5-2fab-4971-bb55-461b94eeee3a","thread_id":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}
{"sender_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","event":"chat","schema_version":2,"history":[{"author_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","content":"We have completed the environment setup for the BIOM5350 CDH17 final project.\n\nNext task: DATA SOURCE FEASIBILITY CHECK ONLY.\n\nResearch question:\nHow does CDH17 RNA expression differ between colorectal tumors, normal colorectal tissues, and other normal human tissues?\n\nPlease investigate publicly accessible RNA-seq expression datasets, prioritizing the UCSC Xena uniformly processed TCGA + GTEx (Toil) data.\n\nTasks:\n1. Identify an exact, accessible dataset containing both TCGA colorectal cancer samples (COAD and READ) and GTEx normal tissue samples.\n2. Verify that CDH17 is present in the expression matrix. Record its gene identifier and whether the dataset uses gene symbols or Ensembl IDs.\n3. Identify the expression normalization/transformation (e.g., TPM, log2(TPM+1)), including any documentation required to interpret the values.\n4. Identify matching sample metadata with sample IDs, study/source, tissue type, tumor/normal designation, and any relevant annotations.\n5. Determine whether COAD/READ tumor samples, TCGA adjacent-normal samples, GTEx colon samples, and other normal tissues can be distinguished reliably.\n6. Investigate whether a small targeted download or API-based extraction of CDH17 expression and associated metadata is possible without downloading a multi-gigabyte matrix.\n7. Report exact dataset names, source URLs, file sizes where available, sample group definitions, and potential batch-effect limitations.\n8. Recommend the most feasible data acquisition method for our CoCalc environment.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Do not download full expression matrices or large files.\n- Do not perform statistical analysis.\n- Do not create figures or implement the analysis pipeline yet.\n- Do not claim a dataset is accessible unless you have verified its endpoint or metadata.\n- Do not overwrite existing project files.\n- Report findings, uncertainty, and source links, then stop for review.","date":"2026-11-25T17:00:41.995Z"}],"date":"2026-11-25T17:00:41.995Z","message_id":"76e5168a-713e-4e75-ae75-ec48f1b3ca3f","thread_id":"a1f6a6c4-739f-4038-8c65-03a0014e0e3e","parent_message_id":"aff019f5-7f20-4441-a265-2ba9f03ae1d5","editing":{},"acp_state":"running"}